# WHAT PRETTIER MAY NOT TOUCH. Every line here decides something — prettier 3
# already honours .gitignore, so build output and scratch directories need no
# entry and none is given.

# EVERY Markdown file, at every depth — not just the root, and not just docs/.
# The plans, decisions, reference notes and the folder READMEs are all
# hand-formatted prose whose tables carry measured figures, and prettier re-pads
# every cell to align its pipes: a one-word edit to one row then rewrites the
# whole block. It also turns `*emphasis*` into
# `_emphasis_`. On files whose value IS the text, that trade is backwards.
*.md

# CAPTURED FROM UPSTREAM, so its shape is the provider's and not ours.
# `assets-sample.json` is a trimmed live capture of
# Inzhur's `/_api/assets` (see packages/core/README.md); reformatting it puts a
# whitespace diff on top of every re-capture and makes the refreshed file fail
# this very check. TWO LINES, NOT ONE `**/__fixtures__/`: infra/src/__fixtures__/
# is formatted on purpose and a widened glob would silently stop checking it.
src/**/__fixtures__/
packages/core/src/**/__fixtures__/

# Machine-written, never hand-edited. One lockfile now that infra/ is a workspace
# member: its npm one is gone with the second installer (*Core is pure*).
pnpm-lock.yaml

# COMMITTED, BUT NOT OURS TO FORMAT. Git tracks four entries under `.claude/` —
# `settings.json`, `agents/`, `commands/`, `skills/` — and they are configuration
# this repository carries rather than source it writes. eslint and vitest already
# exclude the directory whole for the same reason (*Review, gates, tests*), which leaves prettier as
# the ONLY gate that reads them, failing on files nobody edited: `/update-config`
# writes `settings.json` with `JSON.stringify(obj, null, 2)` and no trailing
# newline, and a skill ships `scripts/*.js`, `references/*.json` and `*.yaml` beside
# its Markdown; `settings.json` alone would cover only the first of them.
.claude/

# Machine-written, never hand-edited: `pnpm openapi` emits it with JSON.stringify, whose
# array style differs from prettier's. Left un-ignored, the two merge gates deadlock the first
# time the generator emits an array of short scalars — formatting it fails the drift test, and
# regenerating it fails format:check.
docs/reference/openapi.json
